# Nirnside — non-negotiable rules

Nirnside is a **local-first, out-of-game hub** for The Elder Scrolls Online. It shows
one player's own account (characters, inventory, stickerbook) and a Tamriel
encyclopedia, sourced from in-game data. These rules are hard constraints agreed with
the product owner. Do not relax them without explicit approval.

## 1. Live patch only — never deprecated
- All game data (skills, sets, items, scribing, Champion Points, tooltips, systems)
  MUST match the **current live ESO patch**. As of this writing that is **Update 50 +
  Season One (2026)**; on a new live patch the catalog must be re-ingested, not frozen
  at an old update.
- If something is **removed from the live game, it must not appear in the catalog**.
  (Exception: an item that is no longer obtainable but is still physically sitting in a
  player's bags MUST still render in Inventory — hiding it would make the bag a lie.
  Mark it as unobtainable; do not delete it from the account view.)
- PTS / unreleased data never mixes into the live catalog. If ever added, it lives in a
  clearly separate PTS section.

## 2. Accuracy is sacred
- **In-game data is the source of truth**, above every external source. Order of trust:
  in-game API dump > community DB (ESO-Hub, LibSets) > everything else. If a community
  source conflicts with an in-game value, the in-game value wins.
- Every displayed fact that came from a community source (not verified against an
  in-game dump) MUST be tagged as such (`source: "community"` / "unverified"), never
  presented as confirmed in-game truth.
- **No silent math.** We do not currently compute combat numbers (DPS, mitigation, CP
  diminishing returns, buff stacking). Show as-written tooltips and slotted state only.
  If a calculated value is ever added and cannot be produced correctly, DO NOT guess —
  surface a visible warning to the user instead.
- Missing data is shown as **unknown with a timestamp** (e.g. "not scanned since last
  patch"), never faked as empty or silently hidden.

## 3. Privacy & security — local only
- Nirnside runs **entirely on the user's own machine**. Account data never leaves the
  device. No servers, no accounts, no telemetry, no analytics, no ads.
- Each copy only ever handles **its own player's data**. Never build features that pull
  another player's account data to a place the operator can read it. Any future sharing
  must be end-to-end encrypted such that the host cannot decrypt it.
- Never store or request ESO passwords or credentials. Never inject into, hook, read the
  memory of, or sniff packets from the ESO process. The **only** sanctioned data path is
  the game writing its own `SavedVariables`, which we parse from disk.
- Guild banks: **not collected at all.** House banks: **not collected.**

## 4. Never harm the game / never interrupt play
- The in-game addon(s) MUST NOT do work during combat, and MUST NOT cause lag, frame
  drops, or Lua errors — ever, but especially while playing.
- Snapshots of account/character data happen **only on logout and ReloadUI** (idle
  moments), event-driven, never on a timer during play, never scanning bag events mid-session.
- Heavy full-catalog scans (every item/skill ID in the game) are a **separate, opt-in,
  AFK-only** addon/mode that is never loaded during normal play.
- Only read/write what actually changed. Data that doesn't change every session must not
  be re-scanned or re-written every session (hash / dirty-check first).

## 5. Scope guardrails (current)
- Platform: **PC**. Region: **EU first** (schema keeps NA/megaserver as a flag).
- Language: **English only**.
- In scope: full inventory (IIfA-style, with locations + filters), stickerbook
  (collected vs missing, game-like), character sheets (identity incl. vampire/werewolf
  stage & lines, skills incl. subclassing / Class Mastery / scribing / skill styles,
  Champion Points, equipped incl. back bar, companions, research/motifs/recipes),
  currencies, guilds + trader status, Pithka-style trial/dungeon achievements, and a
  full live encyclopedia.
- Out of scope (for now): combat math, food/potion/buff timers ("currently buffed"),
  guild banks, house banks, mail/buyback/decon, PvP ranks, quest log, outfits/dyes as a
  feature, Tales of Tribute, armory/loadout manager.

## 6. Coherence — one shared catalog
- The account view and the encyclopedia are **one system over one database**, not two
  apps. The same entities (sets, skills, Champion stars, scribing scripts, achievements)
  back both. New features must reuse the catalog, not fork a parallel dataset.
- Everything cross-links **both ways**: an account entity (a worn set, a known skill
  line, a slotted CP star) links to its catalog page, and every catalog page shows the
  player's ownership/knowledge of it.
- Source precedence is enforced in the importer, not by convention: `ingame` >
  `community` > `reference`, merged **field by field** so a partial in-game scan upgrades
  entries without dropping reference detail. Reference seed data must be mechanic-accurate
  and must NOT invent volatile per-patch numbers — leave those empty for the scan to fill.

## 7. Assets & sources
- Only use images/data that are **free and legal** to use, with attribution where
  required. No paid or ToS-violating asset extraction.
- Prefer in-game-derived strings/icons where we already have them from a snapshot;
  otherwise community sources, clearly credited.
